 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“My most humble duty remembered to you, hoping in god of your good health, as I myself am at the making hereof. This is to let you understand that I you child am in a most heavy case by reason of the country, [which] is such that it causeth much sickness, [such] as the scurvy and the bloody flux and diverse other diseases, which maketh the body very poor and weak. . . .</p>\n<p>And I have nothing to comfort me, nor is there nothing to be gotten here but sickness and death, except [in the event] that one had money to lay out in some things for profit. . . .</p>\n<p>[Mr. Jackson] much marvelled that you would send me a servant to the Company; he saith I had been better knocked on the head. And indeed so I find it now, to my great grief and misery; and [I] saith that if you love me you will redeem me suddenly, for which I do entreat and beg. And if you cannot get the merchants to redeem me for some little money, then for God’s sake get a gathering or entreat some good folks to lay out some little sum of money in meal and cheese and butter and beef. Any eating meat will yield great profit.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Letter from an Indentured Servant to his Parents, 1623</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614631,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The practice of indentured servitude in the early English colonies served to",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166497,
     "content_html": "provide labor for silver mines\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166498,
     "content_html": "provide labor for tobacco farms\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166496,
     "content_html": "provide labor for cotton crops\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166495,
     "content_html": "provide labor for factories\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614632,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the author of this letter requesting from his parents?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166502,
     "content_html": "That they either pay off his indenture debt or send supplies he can sell for a profit\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166501,
     "content_html": "That they come visit him\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166500,
     "content_html": "That they send him cheese and beef to eat\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166499,
     "content_html": "That they send him meat and medicine to cure him of disease\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614633,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Why did people come to North America as indentured servants in the seventeenth century? ",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166506,
     "content_html": "There were few opportunities for advancement in England.\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166505,
     "content_html": "Parents needed fewer mouths to feed in difficult economic times.\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166504,
     "content_html": "People thought life would be easier in the New World.\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166503,
     "content_html": "People thought they would become rich.\n"
    }
   ],
